{
  "task_id": "fpp-primary-type-gold",
  "name": "FPP primary_type gold (170, v2)",
  "version": "2026-09-09-v2",
  "id_field": "item_id",
  "instructions": "TYPOLOGY question (random-control sample -- general typing check). Read the Russian event text and choose the ONE category that best fits, under these v2 definitions (see code/prompts/fpp_system_prompt_v2.md for the full spec). No model's answer is shown -- this is a BLIND gold label. IMPORTANT (2026-09-09 decision): a forced resignation or removal with NO stated crime/investigation/court action is governor_political, NOT arrest_legal -- arrest_legal requires the text to state a specific legal/investigative predicate DIRECTED AT the person (a named crime, an opened case, a court action, formal charges, or a finding by a legal/oversight body). Categories: (1) arrest_legal -- a stated legal/investigative predicate against a person, incl. a resignation/removal EXPLICITLY TIED to one. (2) protest -- rallies, pickets, strikes, petitions, collective letters, boycotts; also a protest being denied/dispersed. (3) disaster_accident -- fires, explosions, floods, industrial/transport accidents, disease outbreaks, mass poisonings, any deaths/injuries/ЧП. (4) governor_political -- an official's political/personnel status, statement, or reputation with NO stated legal predicate: plain resignations/dismissals/removals, term expirations, policy-reason firings, reputational scandals, an official as complainant/victim (not accused), general political conflict/maneuvering. (5) election -- campaigns, candidate registration/disqualification, vote results, election-law disputes, election-commission actions. (6) economic -- budget/investment/enterprise/tax/regional-economic news, no legal action, no disaster. (7) social -- healthcare/education/pension/social-services policy or delivery, not itself a protest or disaster. (8) military -- deployments, operations, mobilization, defense-industry news (not accidental incidents -- those are disaster_accident). (9) other -- genuinely fits none of the above 8. If truly torn between two categories with real textual support for both, use the 'Ambiguous' option and say why in Notes -- do not guess.",
  "instructions_by_variant": {
    "binary": "BINARY question (this text was flagged by the classifier as being on the arrest_legal / governor_political boundary). Read ONLY the Russian text below and answer ONE factual question -- do not apply any category scheme and do not think about what label the event should get. Question: does the text ITSELF state that a specific crime, criminal case, investigation, court action, or formal charge has been brought against a named person? 'Yes' requires the text to name or clearly describe such a thing -- a crime, an opened criminal/administrative case, a court decision or sentence, formal charges, or a finding by a prosecutor/oversight body -- directed AT a person. 'No' means the text describes only a resignation, dismissal, removal, term expiration, policy dispute, public statement, or similar political/personnel event, with nothing of that kind stated. 'Unclear' means the TEXT ITSELF is genuinely ambiguous on this specific factual question (not that you are torn between two category labels -- there is no category question here). Use Notes for anything worth flagging.",
    "typology": "TYPOLOGY question (random-control sample -- general typing check). Read the Russian event text and choose the ONE category that best fits, under these v2 definitions (see code/prompts/fpp_system_prompt_v2.md for the full spec). No model's answer is shown -- this is a BLIND gold label. IMPORTANT (2026-09-09 decision): a forced resignation or removal with NO stated crime/investigation/court action is governor_political, NOT arrest_legal -- arrest_legal requires the text to state a specific legal/investigative predicate DIRECTED AT the person (a named crime, an opened case, a court action, formal charges, or a finding by a legal/oversight body). Categories: (1) arrest_legal -- a stated legal/investigative predicate against a person, incl. a resignation/removal EXPLICITLY TIED to one. (2) protest -- rallies, pickets, strikes, petitions, collective letters, boycotts; also a protest being denied/dispersed. (3) disaster_accident -- fires, explosions, floods, industrial/transport accidents, disease outbreaks, mass poisonings, any deaths/injuries/ЧП. (4) governor_political -- an official's political/personnel status, statement, or reputation with NO stated legal predicate: plain resignations/dismissals/removals, term expirations, policy-reason firings, reputational scandals, an official as complainant/victim (not accused), general political conflict/maneuvering. (5) election -- campaigns, candidate registration/disqualification, vote results, election-law disputes, election-commission actions. (6) economic -- budget/investment/enterprise/tax/regional-economic news, no legal action, no disaster. (7) social -- healthcare/education/pension/social-services policy or delivery, not itself a protest or disaster. (8) military -- deployments, operations, mobilization, defense-industry news (not accidental incidents -- those are disaster_accident). (9) other -- genuinely fits none of the above 8. If truly torn between two categories with real textual support for both, use the 'Ambiguous' option and say why in Notes -- do not guess."
  },
